Locator Type Locator Name Syntax id id <code>driver.FindElement(By.Id, 'user-name').SendKeys('standard_user')</code> name name <code>driver.FindElement(By.Name, 'password').SendKeys("secret_sauce")</code> Link text linkText <code>driver.FindElement(By.LinkText, 'Sauce Labs Backpack').Click()</code> Partial link text partialLinkText <code>driver.FindElement(By.PartialLinkText, 'Light').Click()</code> Class name className <code>driver.FindElement(By.ClassName, 'submit-button').Click()</code> Tag name tagName <code>IList&lt;IWebElement&gt; links = driver.FindElements(By.TagName, 'input')</code> Customizable   Locators CSS selector cssSelector <code>driver. FindElement(By.CSS_SELECTOR, 'input#email').send_keys('abhisheksinghcpj@gmail.com')</code> Xpath xpath (See XPath section below for details) <p>Methods used:</p> <ul> <li> <p>To find and use a single element/value, use <code>FindElement()</code>:</p> <p><code>csharp driver.FindElement(By.CssSelector("#app &gt; div &gt; main &gt; article &gt; h3")).Click();</code></p> </li> <li> <p>To find multiple elements/values, use <code>FindElements()</code>:</p> <p><code>csharp driver.FindElements(By.CssSelector("#app &gt; div &gt; main &gt; article &gt; h3"));  //Note: You cannot directly use ".Click()" on FindElements, as it returns a collection.</code></p> </li> </ul> <p>LinkText and Partial LinkText:</p> <ul> <li>We can find an element using the link text or the partial link text in Selenium WebDriver. Both these locators can only be applied to elements with the anchor tag (<code>&lt;a&gt;</code>).</li> <li>The link text locator matches the exact text inside the anchor tag. The partial link text locator matches the text inside the anchor tag partially.</li> <li><code>NoSuchElementException</code> shall be thrown for both these locators if there is no matching element.</li> </ul> <p>Example:</p> <p>Code:</p> <pre><code>driver.FindElement(By.LinkText("click here")).Click();
driver.FindElement(By.PartialLinkText("here")).Click();
</code></pre>
